Subject: [PATCH v7 1/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Say what Dovecot does to a
 reader's write
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: pvpzrzlpmwqlqmxquqwmtoqxmsknovso
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:30:02 +0000

Dovecot opens a mailbox read-only for a login without write rights,
and answers OK to a STORE or EXPUNGE there without changing anything.
The spec said those fail, so a correct build would fail its own
acceptance test.

- The rights section says flags and expunges change nothing, and
  append, copy, and move fail.
- Acceptance step 7 expects the same.
---
change-id: pvpzrzlpmwqlqmxquqwmtoqxmsknovso

 jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org | 12 +++++++-----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org b/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org
index f6b66b50..4ae772d0 100644
--- a/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org
+++ b/jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org
@@ -43,9 +43,11 @@ follows from these rules, and the README states them first.
   one already there.
 - Anyone may read the list over IMAP. Any user name logs in with any
   password, and that login may list, fetch, search, and IDLE, and
-  nothing else. Dovecot's ACL rejects its attempts to set flags,
-  append, copy into a mailbox, move, or expunge, so it cannot archive
-  or delete a message, and it cannot mark one read for anyone else.
+  nothing else. Dovecot's ACL opens every mailbox read-only for it:
+  its attempts to set flags or expunge change nothing, and its
+  attempts to append, copy into a mailbox, or move fail. So it cannot
+  archive or delete a message, and it cannot mark one read for anyone
+  else.
 - IMAP has no anonymous mode, so an agent logs in as its own address,
   such as =claude@p7x.dev=, with any password.
 - Two logins may change the list: =pat@p7x.dev= and =mbsync=. Each
@@ -276,8 +278,8 @@ beastie.
 6. A message with no Message-ID is refused at the end of DATA. msmtp
    exits non-zero and nothing lands on the list.
 7. Logged in as =claude@p7x.dev=, an IMAP STORE of =\Deleted=
-   followed by EXPUNGE on =lists= fails, and so does a MOVE to
-   =Archive=. The message stays in place.
+   followed by EXPUNGE on =lists= changes nothing, and a MOVE to
+   =Archive= fails. The message stays in place, its flags unchanged.
 8. A login as =pat@p7x.dev= with a wrong password fails.
